exports[`the parts a tap opens > the papers of a batch destroyed at the godown (SC-139) 1`] = `
{
  "destruction": "Destruction certificate OCE/DC/26-27/0217 · Orange City Enviro Services DESTROYED For Rakesh Traders, Kalamna Market, Nagpur, Maharashtra · GSTIN 27AABCR1234F1Z5 Munchly Mango Drink 200 ml HSN 2202 · batch MF-2407-111 · best before 15 Sept 2026184 packs Weight food and packaging39.6 kg Method slit open, buried and covered at the authorised municipal landfill15 Sept, 13:20 Agency authorisation MPCB/SWM/NGP/0412Orange City Enviro Services Evidence two photos · Vision's checks 4 of 4approved by Priya Deshmukh Input GST he reverses section 17(5)(h), GSTR-3B Table 4(B)(1)₹133.40 Destroyed at the municipal landfill, Nagpur on expiry day, from Kalamna Market godown. Rakesh Traders reverses the input GST on these packs in GSTR-3B Table 4(B)(1) under section 17(5)(h).",
  "expiry": "Expiry credit note CN/0115 · Munchly Foods → Rakesh Traders NO GST ADJ. 184 packs destroyed at the godown at the ₹14.50 dealer price₹2,668.00 Input GST he reverses on them 5%, section 17(5)(h)₹133.40 Destruction charges Orange City Enviro Services, ₹1.50 a pack₹276.00 Credit to Rakesh Traders₹3,077.40 A financial credit note: no GST is charged or adjusted on it, and Munchly's output tax on the original sale stands. Issued against destruction certificate OCE/DC/26-27/0217; adjusted against Rakesh Traders' account.",
  "itc": "GST ITC memo Section 17(5)(h) · Munchly Foods ITC KEPTPackets sold under tax invoices1,052Destroyed, gifted or lost0Destroyed at Rakesh Traders' godown his stock: he reverses their credit184Input GST kept ₹0.55 a pack, estimated from the cost and the GST rate₹679.80Reversal in GSTR-3B, Table 4(B)(1)none Section 17(5)(h) blocks credit on goods written off, destroyed, lost or given away free. These packs were sold under tax invoices, so it does not apply. The credit would be reversed only if the stock came back under the expiry claim and Munchly destroyed it. Credit on donated units is reversed: 17(5)(h) blocks it on gifts and, since 1 October 2023, 17(5)(fa) on CSR donations.The 184 packs destroyed at Rakesh Traders' godown were his stock, bought under tax invoice: he reverses their input credit, and Munchly Foods keeps its own.",
  "keeps": "Who keeps what Rakesh Traders receives₹15,654 and the expiry credit for 184 packs₹3,077 and the GST he reverses on them and the agency's charges−₹409 and paid 1,236 × ₹14.5, the van and the fee−₹18,322 He ends whole₹0 Expiry claim Munchly avoids₹22,050 Price support it pays instead−₹3,934 and the expiry settlement for 184 packs−₹3,077 Better for Munchly₹15,039₹15,039 The same ₹15,039 swing as the ledger, seen from Munchly's cash: the ₹14.5 credit Rakesh would have claimed and the ₹14.5 he paid cancel out. At plan prices it is ₹4,486 of support and a ₹17,564 swing.",
}
`;

